# ai.wing — NextLight Authorized Retailer

Structural changelog. Every significant architectural decision, feature
addition and layout change is logged here so any change can be traced and
reverted. Newest entries at the top.

---

## [0.7.1] — Ribbon sits lower in the hero

Padding on the ribbon's container reweighted so the spare vertical space goes
**above** it rather than below: `pb-9 pt-4 / sm:pb-12 sm:pt-6 / lg:pb-14 lg:pt-8`
became `pb-5 pt-10 / sm:pb-6 sm:pt-14 / lg:pb-6 lg:pt-16`.

The ribbon now sits near the bottom edge of the hero with just enough
clearance not to look flush. Measured at 1265px: 96px above, **24px below**
(was 56px). At 320px: 56px above, 20px below.

### Measurement note
A first reading reported only 6px of clearance. That was the ribbon's own
`.reveal` still holding `translateY(18px)` — it sits below the fold at a 760px
viewport, so its IntersectionObserver had not fired, and 24 − 18 = 6. Adding
`is-visible` by hand did not help either, because the app window being hidden
freezes the transition and `getComputedStyle` keeps returning the start value.

The reliable way to measure a `.reveal` element's settled position in this
environment is to null out `transition`, `transform` and `opacity` inline,
read, then restore. Worth remembering for any future layout measurement on an
element inside a Reveal.

### Verified
Settled geometry confirmed at both widths, no page overflow at 320px, zero
offenders, 0 broken images. `tsc --noEmit` clean, `next build` static.

---

## [0.7.0] — Stat ribbon, per the reference sites

Asked whether the three stats could be represented another way, with both
reference sites named. Checked them rather than guessing:

- **kineticfiber.us** runs a full-width rounded pill under its hero carrying a
  single line of short claims — roughly 44px tall.
- **bestfiberinternet.us** does the same: a one-line chip row at the base of
  its hero.

Neither uses a tall multi-line card. That was the thing making this element
read as a slab regardless of how the surface was tuned — the problem was the
**form**, not the finish. Four rounds were spent adjusting colour, spacing and
type inside a shape that was wrong to begin with.

### Rebuilt as a slim ribbon
- One line per stat: label inline **before** the value on a shared baseline,
  rather than label above, value below, note under that.
- `items-baseline`, not `items-center` — small caps beside a large figure look
  wrong centred; a shared baseline is what makes the row read as one line.
- The three explanatory notes are gone. Each only restated something the
  subline or the plan cards already said, and they were most of the height.
  `speedNote` and `installNote` removed from `lib/content.ts` rather than left
  as dead data; `priceLabel` added so all three labels sit together.
- Figure scale down again to 1.75/2rem (words 1.45/1.65rem), with
  `PriceLockup`'s `hero` size following, so the value sits comfortably beside
  small caps instead of dominating.

**Height: 172px → 77px**, a little over half. The photograph gains all of it.

### Verified
Ribbon 77px with cells at 76px each; label and value confirmed on one baseline
in all three cells; 56px of photograph below it; hero down from 1005px to
908px. 320px: cells stack, no overflow, figures fit, 0 broken images. No
dangling references to the removed note fields. `tsc --noEmit` clean,
`next build` static.

