## [0.6.3] — Numbers bar spacing and figure balance

Two things left over from 0.6.2.

**The bar was crammed against the trust marks.** Nothing separated the end of
the copy block from the top of the bar, so they read as one run. The bar now
carries its own top padding and the copy block's bottom padding came down to
match, rather than stacking two large gaps. Bottom padding also trimmed, so
the band of asphalt below the bar does not run on.

Measured at 1280px: 82px from the trust marks to the bar, 30px from the bar to
the bottom of the hero. Both were near zero and near 100px respectively.

**A word was set at numeral size.** "Included" at the same size as "8 Gig"
simply filled its cell and shouted over the price, which is the figure that
should lead the row. Added `.stat-figure--word`, a smaller step applied when
the value does not begin with a digit — tested on the value itself rather than
hard-coded to the install cell, so a future rail entry sizes itself correctly.

Whole scale came down one notch at the same time (2.5/3rem → 2.25/2.75rem),
with `PriceLockup`'s `hero` size following, so the rate and the speed figure
stay on the same footing.

Result at 1280px: price 44px, "8 Gig" 44px, "Included" 33px. Cells 160px each.

### Verified
Cells equal at 160px; figures fit without overflow at 320px (36px and 28px
there); no page overflow, 0 broken images. `tsc --noEmit` clean, `next build`
static.

