## [0.3.1] — Photography delivered and wired in

All five images supplied. Every slot from 0.3.0 is now filled; no component
needed changing to accept them, which was the point of building the manifest
first.

### Assets were reprocessed before use
Delivered at ~8 MB each (~35 MB total) against a ~400 KB brief, and the social
card arrived as `og-image.png` rather than `.jpg`. Originals are preserved in
the session scratchpad under `images-original/`.

- Re-encoded with sharp at JPEG q80, progressive, mozjpeg.
  **35 MB → 632 KB total**, no visible quality loss — the sources were
  enormously over-encoded, not high-detail.
- `og-image.png` converted to `og-image.jpg`, cover-cropped to 1200x630, the
  1.91:1 ratio social platforms expect. The `.png` was removed.

### Manifest dimensions corrected
Every image came back **1408x768**, not the per-slot sizes specified — the
generator uses a fixed 16:9 output. `lib/images.ts` was updated to the real
dimensions. This matters: `next/image` reserves layout space from these
numbers, and wrong values cause layout shift and distortion.

### Hero backdrop made responsive — the one real problem
A 16:9 photograph cannot fill the hero on a narrow screen. Measured crop, via
`scale = max(boxW/imgW, boxH/imgH)`:

| Viewport | Hero box | Upscale | Photo width still visible |
|---|---|---|---|
| 320px | 320x1324 | 1.72x | **13%** |
| 753px | 753x854 | 1.11x | 48% |
| 1009px | 1009x920 | 1.20x | 60% |
| 1265px | 1265x899 | 1.17x | 77% |

At 320px the photo is blown up 1.7x showing a thin vertical slice — it reads
as broken. So the backdrop now renders from `md` upward only; below that the
gradient canvas carries the hero exactly as it did before any photo existed.
`sizes="(max-width: 767px) 640px, 100vw"` stops narrow viewports fetching a
large variant they will not display. `object-position: 65% 50%` biases the
crop toward the houses, which sit right of centre in the frame.

The three band photos are unaffected — they sit in a half-width column whose
box tracks the image's own aspect, so there is no crop problem there.

### Scrim retuned
The 0.3.0 scrim (radial at 0.88 plus a heavy linear) buried the photograph
almost completely. Now: radial drops to `md:opacity-50` as a brand tint, a
left-weighted linear (`from-navy-dark via-navy-dark/80 to-navy-dark/25`) holds
contrast under the headline, and an extra `bg-navy-dark/40` applies between md
and lg where the copy still spans most of the width.

### Verified
- 4 images on the page, **0 broken**, `og:image` tag now present.
- 320px: hero photo wrapper computes to `display: none`, all 3 band photos
  present, `scrollWidth === clientWidth === 320`, zero offenders.
- Desktop: hero photo `display: block`, 1024x558 variant served, 60% of frame
  visible, `object-position: 65% 50%`.
- Feature bands balance well — image box 564x308 against text boxes of
  316/342/316, and image-left / image-right alternation confirmed.
- `tsc --noEmit` clean, `next build` static.

### Note for larger displays
1408px is modest for a full-bleed hero backdrop; above ~1400px wide it
upscales. It sits under a 50% scrim at low contrast so softness does not read,
but a 2400px-wide source would be better if the hero is ever re-shot.

