## [0.3.0] — Photography slots wired ahead of the assets

### Copy
- Fiber section: "Residential fiber plans with transparent pricing" →
  **"Residential fiber plans and monthly rates"** ("transparent" dropped).
- Why NextLight: "Community-owned fiber, engineered for consistent
  performance" → **"Fiber to the home, owned by the community"**
  ("engineered" and "consistent" dropped).

### `lib/images.ts` — the image manifest
Photography was commissioned but not yet delivered, so the slots were built
first and made inert rather than left as a later retrofit.

Every photograph is declared once in `images`, with its exact required
filename and intrinsic dimensions. `resolve(key)` checks `public/<src>` with
`fs.existsSync` and returns `null` when the file is absent. Because every
consumer is a server component, this runs **at build time only** — no runtime
cost, nothing in the client bundle.

The effect: a missing photo is never a broken image or a 404. The consuming
component simply renders its image-free layout, and the slot fills itself on
the next build once the file is dropped in. Photos can land one at a time.

Server-only module — must not be imported from a `'use client'` component.

### Slots
| Key | File | Size | Where |
|---|---|---|---|
| `heroBackground` | `hero-background.jpg` | 2400×1400 | Behind the hero, under the navy scrim |
| `installation` | `fiber-installation.jpg` | 1600×1200 | Feature band 1 |
| `household` | `family-streaming.jpg` | 1600×1200 | Feature band 2 |
| `workFromHome` | `work-from-home.jpg` | 1600×1200 | Feature band 3 |
| `openGraph` | `og-image.jpg` | 1200×630 | `og:image` metadata |

### `components/FeatureBands.tsx` — new section
Alternating photograph/copy blocks, the pattern the brand uses on its own
pages. Filters to bands whose photo exists and **returns `null` when none do**,
so the section is absent rather than empty. Band order alternates image-left /
image-right automatically off the index. Copy lives in `featureBands` in
`lib/content.ts`, keeping the single-source-of-truth rule intact.

Placed between the fine-print grid and How It Works — it gives the page a
visual break after the dense comparison table without disturbing the canonical
service-line order.

### Hero backdrop
`BrandCanvas` now renders a `next/image` fill layer when `heroBackground`
resolves, with `priority` set since it is the LCP element. Two scrims stack on
top: the existing navy radial (dropped to 0.88 opacity when a photo is behind
it) plus a left-weighted linear gradient, so the ivory headline keeps contrast
against whatever the photograph is doing. With no photo the radial is simply
the background, exactly as before.

### `og:image`
Added conditionally. A tag pointing at a missing file is worse than no tag, so
the key is omitted from the `openGraph` object entirely until the file exists.

### Brief
`public/images/README.md` carries the filenames, dimensions and the generation
prompts, including the realism constraints and a shared negative list. The
hero prompt specifies a composition with the left half kept visually quiet,
because the headline sits there.

### Verified
`featureBandsRendered: false`, `document.images.length: 0`, zero broken
images, no `og:image` tag — all correct for the pre-delivery state.
`tsc --noEmit` clean, `next build` static.

