## [0.2.1] — Copy pass, hero spacing, sticky-header bug fix

### Sticky header was never sticky (regression from 0.1.0, now fixed)
`html, body { overflow-x: hidden }` — added in 0.1.0 as the 320px overflow
guard — turns `body` into a scroll container, and that silently disables
`position: sticky` for every descendant. The top chrome had been scrolling
away with the page since the first build. Measured before the fix:
`chromeTop: -255` at `scrollY: 255`.

Fixed by switching the guard to `overflow-x: clip`, which trims the same
overflow without establishing a scroll container. After: `chromeTop: 0` at
`scrollY: 1199` on desktop and `scrollY: 1049` at 320px, with `scrollWidth`
still equal to `clientWidth` at both widths.

**Rule for this file: never use `overflow-x: hidden` on `html` or `body`
here — it will break the top chrome again. Use `clip`.**

`--header-offset` was also 130px against a measured mobile chrome of 137px,
so anchored headings landed 7px under the bar. Raised to 140px; the md+ value
of 100px matches its measured 97px.

### Copy professionalised
All rewrites landed in `lib/content.ts` only — no component touched.

| Where | Now reads |
|---|---|
| Hero H1 | "Symmetrical 100% fiber internet with **no data caps.**" |
| Hero subline | Rewritten to match; "fiber to the premises", "annual term agreement" |
| ZIP button | "Check availability" (was "Check") |
| ZIP label | "Confirm service at your address" — reworded to avoid repeating the button |
| Fiber section | "Residential fiber plans with transparent pricing" |
| Bundles | "Internet, managed WiFi and voice bundles" |
| Fine print | "Monthly rates, equipment and included services" |
| Why NextLight | "Community-owned fiber, engineered for consistent performance" |

The hero subline was not on the request list but sits directly under the H1,
so it was rewritten too rather than left tonally mismatched.

The Why NextLight description previously ended "...not fiber to a cabinet down
the street." That clause was dropped rather than reworded: it reads as a
comparison against other operators, which the brief prohibits. The paragraph
now describes only NextLight's own build.

### Hero spacing
Top padding reduced from `pt-14 sm:pt-20 lg:pt-24` to
`pt-8 sm:pt-11 lg:pt-14`, closing the gap to the navbar. Bottom padding
unchanged so the numbers rail keeps its breathing room.

### Verified
- Header sticks at both 320px and desktop.
- 320px: `scrollWidth === clientWidth === 320`, zero offenders (the hero's
  decorative sweep is excluded — it is clipped by the hero's own
  `overflow-hidden`).
- "Check availability" fits: 272px stacked at 320px, 200px beside a 352px
  input at 640px. No overflow at either.
- ZIP checker still resolves — 80503 returns the serviceable message.
- `next build` static, `tsc --noEmit` clean.

