## [0.2.0] — Palette roles corrected, hero rebuilt

### Why
Screenshots of the live mynextlight.com were supplied. The hex values in 0.1.0
were already correct, but their **roles** were wrong. Corrected against the
live site:

| Element | 0.1.0 (wrong) | 0.2.0 (matches brand) |
|---|---|---|
| Page background | `#FFFFFF` white | **`#FFFFF6` ivory** — the site is never pure white |
| Primary button | navy fill, ivory text | **sprout `#D6F38E` fill, navy-dark text** (their "Get Connected") |
| Button shape | `rounded-lg` | **`rounded-full` pill** |
| Top utility bar | navy-dark | **teal `#3ECEBA`** |
| Headings | mixed case, navy-dark | **UPPERCASE, navy `#004A81`** |
| Footer | navy-dark, uniform | **navy `#004A81` + sprout legal bar** with navy text |
| Alternating sections | white / navy-050 | **ivory / white** |
| Section accents | navy-050 tints | **teal tints, sprout pills** |

`navy-050/100/700` survive only as incidental tints. `--color-sand` (`#CBB398`)
and `--color-sun` (`#F9F923`, the sprout hover state) were added to complete
the palette. A `.heading-brand` utility carries the uppercase treatment so the
casing is one declaration rather than a class repeated across components.

### Hero rebuilt
The boxed white order card read as a template, so it is gone. The hero is now
three bands on the navy canvas:
1. **Headline band** — eyebrow pill, oversized uppercase H1 with the closing
   phrase in sprout green, subline, then the ZIP checker inline (a single
   ivory pill with a sprout Check button, stacking below 640px), then trust
   marks as a plain check row rather than chips-in-boxes.
2. **Numbers rail** — a three-cell `<dl>` divided by hairlines: the price
   lockup in sprout, top speed and installation in teal. This is where the
   price anchor now lives.
3. **Brand canvas** — a navy radial wash plus one static two-stroke sweep in
   sprout and teal, echoing the flowing line in NextLight's own material.
   Fixed, `aria-hidden`, no motion, no 3D.

`hero.headline` was split into `headline` + `headlineAccent` and a `statRail`
block was added, so the accent phrase and every rail label stay in
`lib/content.ts` rather than being hard-coded in the layout.

### Call button removed from the hero
Requested directly. This reverses the 0.1.0 brief, which had required a hero
call button — noting it here because the two instructions conflict and the
later one was taken as current. The call path is unaffected: the sticky header
call button is on screen for the whole session, and every plan card still ends
in a "Call to order" CTA. Hero `tel:` anchors: 0. Page total dropped 12 → 11.

### Verified after the change
- Computed styles sampled across 18 elements — every one returns an exact
  brand hex (`#FFFFF6`, `#D6F38E`, `#3ECEBA`, `#004A81`, `#002C51`).
- 320px: `scrollWidth === clientWidth === 320`, no page overflow. Three
  elements report wider than the viewport: the decorative hero sweep and its
  two paths, which are intentionally oversized and clipped by the hero's
  `overflow-hidden`.
- CTA labels, `data-call-cta` coverage (11/11), section order and the
  banned-phrase sweep all still pass. `next build` static.

